 ],
 "literal": "Rumors how will they cease, O friend! By the great ocean's / fish-smelling wide shore, even though the charioteer restrained [it], / without stopping, passed by, the clattering swift chariot, / did I see [it] or did I not, at midnight? / On the high white sand, from the low-hanging punnai tree, / pollen-filled excellent flowers plucking, / the playmates all together saw [it] indeed!",
 "translation": "How will the rumors ever cease, my friend? Even though the charioteer tried to restrain it, his swift, clattering chariot sped past without stopping along the wide, fish-smelling shore of the great ocean. Did I see it or did I not, in the dead of night? But my playmates, who were plucking pollen-filled, beautiful flowers from the low branches of the punnai tree on the high white dunes, saw it all together!",
 "modern": "தோழியே! பெரிய கடலின் புலால் நாற்றம் வீசும் அகன்ற துறையில், பாகன் தடுத்து நிறுத்தவும் நில்லாமல் வேகமாகச் சென்ற ஒலியெழுப்பும் கடிய தேர், நள்ளிரவில் சென்றதை நான் பார்த்தேனோ இல்லையோ? ஆனால், உயர்ந்த வெண்மையான மணல் குன்றில் தாழ்ந்த புன்னை மரத்தின் தாதுக்கள் நிறைந்த மலர்களைக் கொய்து கொண்டிருந்த என் தோழியர் கூட்டம் முழுவதும் அதனை ஒருசேரப் பார்த்துவிட்டதே! இனி இந்த அலர் எவ்வாறு அடங்கும்?",
 "explanation": "The heroine speaks to her confidante in deep anxiety about the rumors spreading in their coastal village. Her lover had visited her secretly at midnight, but his swift chariot made a loud clattering sound as it sped along the shore. Although the charioteer tried to guide it quietly, the noise was unmistakable. The heroine wonders in confusion whether she actually witnessed his arrival in the darkness of midnight or if it was a dream. However, her playmates, who were awake plucking flowers from the low-hanging branches of the punnai tree on the sand dunes, witnessed the chariot's passage together. This public sighting has triggered widespread rumors (alar) in the village, making their secret love affair difficult to conceal and prompting the need for an early marriage.",
